# The yaml-test-suite fixtures are byte-exact test data. Line endings are part
# of what those cases check -- several distinguish \n from \r\n inside block
# scalars -- so git must not translate them on checkout. Without this, the
# semantic conformance test fails on Windows, where core.autocrlf is on by
# default and the fixtures arrive with CRLF.
tests/testthat/fixtures/** -text

# C sources keep LF on every platform; R CMD check inspects their line endings.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
